<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Build Lab: Prove the Move</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~15 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        A refactor is only finished when you can show that nothing changed. Four checks, in this
        order:
    </p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Check</th><th>What it proves</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Collect a coin</td>
            <td>The coin branch reaches the manager. Console says <code>Coins: 1</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Walk into a spike</td>
            <td>The signed amount still hurts. Console says <code>Health: 2</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Pick up a potion at full health</td>
            <td>The ceiling travelled with the value. Health stays at <code>3</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Take damage until death</td>
            <td><code>Die()</code> runs from inside <code>ChangeHealth</code>. Health is back at max, coins are halved.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="callout trap">
        <strong>A refactor that also changes behaviour is not a refactor.</strong> If the jump feels
        different, the movement is slower, or a pickup stopped working while you were in these files,
        you touched something that was not part of the move. Put it back and commit the move on its
        own — a commit that says "moved stats to StatManager" should contain nothing else.
    </div>
</div>

